is commutative. By\nCriteria for Representability,\nLemma <REF_0011>\nthe left vertical arrow is surjective, flat, and locally of finite\npresentation. Consider\n<MATH_0024>\nAs <MATH_0025> is locally of finite type, we see that the base change\n<MATH_0026> is locally of finite type. Moreover,\n<MATH_0027> is\nsurjective, flat, and locally of finite presentation as a base change of\n<MATH_0028>. Thus\n<MATH_0029>\nis an fppf covering of algebraic spaces, and we conclude that\n<MATH_0030> is locally of finite type by\nDescent on Spaces, Lemma\n<REF_0012>.\nBy definition this means that <MATH_0031> is locally of finite type (because the\nvertical arrow <MATH_0032> is smooth\nas a base change of <MATH_0033> and surjective as <MATH_0034> has\nonly one point). Since <MATH_0035> we see that (3) holds.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nIt is clear that (3) implies (2).\nIf (2) holds then <MATH_0036> is a finite type point of <MATH_0037> by\nLemma <REF_0013>\nand\nLemma <REF_0014>\nto see that <MATH_0038> is nonempty, i.e., the\nunique point of <MATH_0039> is a finite type point of <MATH_0040>.\n<STRUCT_0004>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:af46163063c54f5f9fcae20572c8a1f95cb844febda37a5ddc0ce5ffe5821154", "unit_id": "inventory:stacks-morphisms:06G3:proof/0001"}}}], "input_freeze": {"hash": "sha256:13279688cef2c0a8aa16103c0f5027a469640935823074949ef2256df96a4ffa", "path": "translation-data/source-adoption-inputs/p0-101-stacks-morphisms-p011-r04.json"}, "model_output": {"hash": "sha256:37ded9398e344568e71bd8f061e5ecef06d849ff675b6fd899917c8b5cf492f0", "path": "docs/evidence/p0-101-stacks-morphisms-p011-r04-raw-01.jsonl", "record_hash": "sha256:a82f771842647c9c5a85f607f396e6e3beb1d2716cd2d16035b0414e775b912d"}, "neighbor_unit_ids": ["tag:06G3:statement"], "policy_revision": "git:47a3fd756322c92b986732a1a673c94462f5c165", "prior_generations": [], "prompt_version": "translator-v2", "source_adoption_id": "p0-101-stacks-morphisms-p011-r04", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afce